# The bgSetScrollX pattern: a u8 parameter used as an array index and as
# a shift count. After `pha` the count must be read 2 bytes above the slot
# it was stored to (ported from opensnes-emu test_variable_shift_u8_compound).
# The offsets below are today's frame layout: if a frame change moves them,
# re-derive "shift load = zero-extended bg store + 2" before updating.
# u8: bg is zero-extended into 10,s, the shift reads it back at 12,s.
in set_scroll_u8: present and\.w #\$00FF\n\tsta 10,s
in set_scroll_u8: present lda\.w #1\n\tpha\n\tlda 12,s\n\ttax\n\tpla\n\tcpx #0\n\tbeq \+\n-\tasl a
# u16: bg stays in its parameter slot, 24,s (36 before the slot colouring
# of 2026-09-27 shrank the frame); after pha it is 26,s.
in set_scroll_u16: present lda\.w #1\n\tpha\n\tlda 26,s\n\ttax\n\tpla\n\tcpx #0
# The array store: X is the index, the value is loaded after it (indexed
# long since 2026-10-08; a pha / tax / pla around `sta.l $0000,x` before).
in set_scroll_u8: present tax\n\tlda \d+,s\n\tsta\.l scroll_x,x
# cpx #0 needs 16-bit index assembly.
present \.INDEX 16
